cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. It is an experimental research toolkit; its results are simulation results under the stated configurations, not empirical findings about any system outside the simulation."
type: software
title: "XENO ZIRAN SIMULATOR runtime: operational-shape simulation and experimental instruments for comparing configurations"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Fujie"
    given-names: "Naoto"
# repository-code: add the public repository URL when it is published
# No DOI has been assigned. If a DOI is issued later, add it here as `doi:`.
abstract: >-
  A runtime for simulating how differences ignite, propagate, are retained and reconfigure connections across a
  field of configurations, with experimental instruments for varying scale, topology, memory, coupling, horizon,
  boundary and observation resolution, ablating runtime mechanisms, operating on retained history (fork, removal,
  reactivation, migration) and comparing the results with paired seeds, noise replicates and recorded provenance.
  The instruments compare configurations; they are not an implementation of a final ontology.
keywords:
  - simulation
  - complex systems
  - operational shape
  - ablation
  - reproducibility
